{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CI Verified -1 on all four changes in this stack was NOT caused by any of them. Root-caused\nrather than rechecked, per the flaky-test rule; recording it here because it will hit anyone\nelse with an open patchset right now.\n\nSIGNATURE: only the macos-latest/py3.13 cell failed; all three ubuntu cells passed. pytest\nexited 5 ('no tests collected') with 'no tests ran in 55.52s' — no collection error, no\ntraceback, no timeout.\n\nMECHANISM — a workflow/tree skew. The Verified lane resolves the reusable workflow from\nTRUSTED main (Uses: _build-and-test.yml@refs/heads/main) while checking out the PATCHSET's\ntree. Commit 920492b1b2f7 ('Reduce macOS pytest cell to platform-compat subset') split its\ncontract across both halves: the workflow now passes -m 'platform_compat and not external'\n(_build-and-test.yml:652), but the marker is auto-applied at collection time by a path-fragment\ntable in tests/conftest.py:198-252 — which lives in the TREE. Any patchset whose parent\npredates that merge therefore gets a workflow asking for a marker no test in its tree can\ncarry: empty selection, exit 5.\n\nEVIDENCE it is not the change: 6 recent macOS jobs show exit 5 across FOUR unrelated Gerrit\nchanges (fix(reads), Pin ticket reads, fix(autodeploy), feat(mcp)); ZERO macOS jobs exited 5\nbefore 920492b1b2f7 merged at ~02:04 UTC. The fault tracks that merge time, not any\npatchset's content. This stack was based on 95387192861c — the commit immediately before it.\n\nREMEDY: rebase, NOT recheck. A recheck re-runs the same stale tree and fails identically.\nRebased all four onto origin/main 537456586d45; the macOS selection now collects 909 tests\ninstead of 0, confirming both the diagnosis and the fix. Re-verified on the new base: 110/110\nof the affected tests pass, make lint and make typecheck clean.\n\nWORTH NOTING FOR THE OWNERS OF 920492b1b2f7: the parity guard that change advertises\n(test_ci_workflow_parity.py) also lives in the tree, so it cannot fire on a patchset that\npredates it — the guard is blind to exactly the skew it exists to catch. Not filing a ticket\nagainst it from here since it is outside this bug's scope, but it will keep biting every open\nchange until each is rebased."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787717496157619001,"uuid":"1e577d86-3efa-4954-8f56-bc13be398b4b"}